{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pocky-l/diegesis/main/docs/schema/scene.schema.json",
  "$comment": "Farm & Charm's crafting bowl, as its own renderer draws it: x and z 3..13, 8 px deep, open, its whisk resting with its loops in the bowl and its handle out over the -x rim. The scene faces the cook; the code turns the bowl back to the world's sides (node bowl), so it stands as the block does from any side, and the scene is the bowl in the world wherever it is drawn. What goes in comes over from the hand: what is thrown in lies as itself, a few of a stack, and the whisk pushes it about; liquids are poured, eggs cracked, flour shaken out. The whisk is taken by its handle (and only there) with a click and goes where the mouse goes. The mixture rises and thickens as it is whisked; once done, what it became shows on the badge to the right, where a click takes it. Camera, badge and book as at the cooking pot (the bowl is as wide), the camera 14 degrees steeper about the same target and the badge and the book turned with it: the bowl is deep and what lies on its floor near the front wall must be seen.",
